   "source": [
    "For null handling, we implemented targeted data hygiene steps to improve consistency and model readiness while minimizing information loss. For Google Analytics, we coerced items to an empty array when missing and backfilled display fields (device_mobile_brand_name, event_page_name, event_page_title) with neutral placeholders (“Other”/“Unknown”), ensuring schema stability for downstream array operations, dashboards, and joins without discarding events. We dropped orders rows lacking required keys (material_id, sales_office_id) and customers rows missing distribution_mode, because these fields are essential for segmentation, joins, and channel attribution; retaining them would introduce ambiguity and leakage. In materials, we consolidated missing beverage_category under a catch-all “Other” to preserve records while preventing category sparsity. Finally, we filtered visit_plan to keep only records with a non-null sales_office, reflecting its role as a mandatory routing/aggregation dimension. Collectively, these changes favor imputation for descriptive fields and strict removal where identifiers are critical, balancing data integrity with coverage."
   ]
