    "## Modelling Plan\n",
    "\n",
    "Now that the EDA is complete, the next step is to predict cart abandonment using patterns observed across device type, event behavior, and order timing. Our goal is to identify which customers are likely to abandon their carts and why they are doing so. One approach we may take is to create a binary target: abandonment. Essentially, abandonment occurs when a customer adds to cart but doesn’t order before their cutoff. Possible features include:\n",
    "Behavioral: event sequences, device type, browsing depth\n",
    "Operational: frequency, anchor day, cutoff time\n",
    "Customer/Product: trade channel, category, and item mix\n",
    "We could start with Logistic Regression for interpretability, then maybe move to Random Forest/XGBoost for better accuracy. Performance could be measured using AUC, Precision/Recall, and Lift charts, with segmentation by device and sales office.\n",
    "\n",
    "For the financial aspect of the modeling cart abandonment, we could combine data from the google_analytics, sales, and materials tables. The google_analytics data shows how customers interact with carts, while the sales and materials data link those behaviors to actual revenue and product details. To measure how abandonment affects revenue, models such as linear regression or elastic net regression could be used to show how changes in abandonment rates relate to total revenue. More advanced models like random forest or gradient boosting can help capture more complex relationships between behavior, timing, and financial outcomes. If time trends matter, time series regression can show how cart abandonment impacts revenue over days or weeks. To study how abandonment changes the product mix, models such as multinomial logistic regression can show how likely certain products are to be abandoned or purchased. Clustering methods like K-Means can group customers or products with similar behaviors, while association rule mining can find relationships between abandoned items and those eventually bought.\n",
    " \n",
    "Overall, these approaches will help explain why cart abandonment happens and how much revenue is potentially lost from abandoned carts. We feel prepared after this EDA to explore insights that will help guide Swire’s decision-making around cart abandonment"
   ]
